          {
            "id": "refresh_procedure",
            "text": "To refresh the status of an application, reopen the same application and its task from a permitted list or entry, selecting the intended task if more than one matches. Wait for the new read to finish; if it fails, is denied, or does not match, the refresh is unconfirmed. Then confirm the application number and task, and read the returned application status separately from the workflow position or any historical decision. Record the observation time, keeping any business update time reported by the source separate — a later read does not by itself prove the record changed. There is no dedicated Refresh button; focusing an already open page does not prove a new read, and no business action should be used to refresh.",
            "quoteIndexes": [
              1,
              2,
              3
            ],
            "requirementIds": [
              "attribute_3"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "verify_discrepancy",
            "text": "To verify a reported status discrepancy, keep both values together with the page, field, selected object and task, role or view, and observation time, labelling any value you have not observed as reported or unavailable. Verify the same typed business object and the relevant task through the current permitted mapping — similar references are not enough — and compare the same field meaning, since the application lifecycle, workflow position, completed-task decision, and payment or other-module status are distinct facts. Re-read the same authorized detail and compare scope, applicable version and times. If disagreement remains without a verified reconciliation rule, retain both findings and the unresolved points rather than automatically preferring a list, a detail view, a later capture, or a prior answer.",
